  "description": "1. MAIN ENTRANCE DOOR: The existing access door along Colebrooke Row is a metal framed sliding glass door. It is proposed to replace this door with a single timber door within a timber surround.\n2. RENDER TO EXTERNAL LOWER GROUND FIRE ESCAPE STAIRCASE: The existing brickwork to the lower ground area is damaged. It is proposed to protect the existing brickwork with a suitable exterior quality render.\n3. SECONDARY ENTRANCE DOORS: The three existing metal framed glazed doors on Colebrooke Place are to be replaced with new metal doors within the existing opening. This is predominantly for aesthetic and security reasons.\n4. LOWER GROUND FLOOR WINDOWS: Along Colebrooke Place there are currently three windows and a bricked up ‘window’ at lower ground floor level. It is proposed to open up the bricked up ‘window’ and install a new window to match the two larger adjacent windows. It is also proposed to replace the other smaller window to match this new window.\n5. NEW ROOF LIGHTS: It is proposed to install four new ‘Conservation Area Rooflights’ on the two long elevations to bring light into the mezzanine level below. The roof light frames will be low profile and black in colour to blend into the existing roof finish.\n",
